{
  "configuration_id": "config_002",
  "reason": "The strongest result so far is config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, resnet50, avgpool, concat → 0.619), which jumps ~9 points over the singleprofile multimodal baseline (0.527). However, we cannot yet decompose whether this multiprofile gain is driven primarily by better RNA aggregation (avgpool over multiple profiles) or by a synergistic interaction between multiprofile RNA and the image branch. Image-only performance is very weak (0.208), suggesting the image signal is limited, but we have no direct evidence for its marginal contribution in the multiprofile regime. config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) is a clean ablation that removes only the image branch while keeping the RNA encoder, profile setting, and aggregation identical to config_018. If rna_only multiprofile approaches 0.58–0.60, the image adds little and future budget should target RNA encoder improvements (scvi, scgpt); if it stays near 0.50, the image still contributes meaningfully and image-encoder upgrades become worthwhile. This single experiment resolves the most important architectural uncertainty and will efficiently direct all subsequent choices under the limited budget."
}

